  "priorExpiration": "2016-01-12",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3217.04 Outside Rear View Mirrors.\n\n(a) A vehicle shall be rejected if the left hand outside rear view mirror or the right hand outside mirror, if so equipped:\n\n(1) Is not in the correct location on the vehicle;\n\n(2) Is not firmly mounted;\n\n(3) Has cracks;\n\n(4) Extends to the left of the vehicle body more than necessary; or\n\n(5) Does not afford a clear view of the road to the rear of the vehicle.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes at Chapter Heading Saf-C 3200) #8915, eff 6-22-07, EXPIRED: 6-22-15\n\nNew. #10886, INTERIM, eff 7-16-15, EXPIRES: 1-12-16; ss by #11016, eff 1-6-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3200.html"
